# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Biggy Smallz Spitmasters — environment configuration
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in the values. `.env.local` is
# git-ignored and read ONLY on the server (the Book a Date API route). The keys
# below never reach the browser.
#
#   cp .env.local.example .env.local
#
# On Vercel, add the same variables under Project → Settings → Environment
# Variables (do not commit real keys).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Where booking emails are sent. This is Biggy's inbox.
OWNER_EMAIL="hello@biggysmallzspitmasters.co.za"

# Which email provider the /api/book route uses. One of: web3forms | resend
# Default is web3forms (simplest — no domain verification required).
EMAIL_PROVIDER="web3forms"

# ── Option A: Web3Forms (default) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# The Book a Service form submits DIRECTLY to Web3Forms from the browser, not
# through our own /api/book route. Web3Forms' free tier blocks server-to-
# server calls with a Cloudflare challenge (see their docs: "It is
# recommended that you use the API client/browser side, not server side.
# Server side usage requires paid plan + server IP whitelisting.") -- so the
# key has to be a NEXT_PUBLIC_ var, baked into the client bundle at build
# time. Web3Forms themselves say this key is public and safe to ship in
# client-side code.
#
# 1. Create a free access key at https://app.web3forms.com (verify the email
#    you want bookings to land in -- Biggy's inbox, ideally).
# 2. Drop the key in BOTH vars below (same value). On Vercel, add it under
#    Project -> Settings -> Environments -> Production, then redeploy --
#    env var changes don't apply to a deployment that's already built.
NEXT_PUBLIC_WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY=""
WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY=""

# ── Option B: Resend ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. Create an API key at https://resend.com/api-keys
# 2. Verify a sending domain, then set RESEND_FROM to an address on it.
RESEND_API_KEY=""
RESEND_FROM="Biggy Smallz Spitmasters <bookings@biggysmallzspitmasters.co.za>"
